Package: FACEHD
Type: Package
Title: FACE-HD: Federated Adaptive Causal Estimation in High Dimensions
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2026-02-13
Authors@R: 
    person("Sinian", "Zhang", 
           email = "zhan9381@umn.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Implements federated learning algorithms for causal inference in 
    multi-site settings. The package estimates the POTENTIAL OUTCOME MEAN at 
    the target site: mu^a_t = E_t[Y(a)] for a in {0, 1}. This is NOT the ATE; 
    to compute ATE = E[Y(1) - Y(0)], run the algorithm twice with a=1 and a=0.
    The package provides two-round and one-round communication protocols with 
    two-level cross-fitting for enhanced robustness against overfitting bias.
    Key features include:
    - Doubly robust estimators with calibrated loss functions for Neyman Orthogonality
    - Optimal aggregation of site-specific estimators via variance minimization
    - Support for GLM families (binomial, gaussian)
    - C++ acceleration for coordinate descent and cross-validation
    - Comparison methods including target-only, sample-size weighted, 
      inverse-variance weighted, and tilted AIPW estimators
